  "question": {
    "text": "In the circuit of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></math> amplifier, a silicon transistor is used. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">V</mtext><mtext>CC</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>V</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">R</mtext><mtext>L</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>k</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math> , collector voltage <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>V</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>.</mo></math> Then the base resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></math> should be ------ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math> (Take input voltage drop across Si transistor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0.7</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> )<br />\n<img src=\"assets\\qt0012_20d593068578.png\" style=\"width:1.92708in;height:1.86042in\" />"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3.86",
  "solution": {
